SUMMARY:[現場] Lunchtime Curator Talk | Solid Pictures
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center\, Pigott Family Gallery (142)
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-lunchtime-curator-talk-solid-
 pictures
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-lunchtime-curator-tal
 k-solid-pictures\n報名/票券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/solidpictu
 res1210\n\n​Join Patrick R. Crowley\, Associate Curator of European Art\
 , on this special highlights tour of Solid Pictures.\n\nBefore 3D printing
 \, there was photosculpture. Curated by Patrick R. Crowley\, Associate Cur
 ator of European Art\, Solid Pictures is the first major exhibition to exp
 lore these largely overlooked objects first conceived in 1859 by the twent
 y-nine-year-old French artist and inventor François Willème. Employing p
 rojection technologies and mechanical instruments\, Willème and his team 
 of operators translated photographic negatives into solid figures across a
  variety of media\, aiming to create affordable portrait sculpture for the
  burgeoning middle class of Second Empire France. Though commercially unsu
 ccessful\, these experiments laid the groundwork for the scanning\, machin
 ing\, and printing technologies ubiquitous today. Bringing together these 
 rare artifacts\, the exhibition opens up a little-known chapter of history
  to reveal the roots and richness of our contemporary world. An accompanyi
 ng catalogue features four newly commissioned essays accompanied by previo
 usly unpublished documentation\, deepening our understanding of this overl
 ooked chapter in the history of art and technology.\n\nRSVP here.\n\n_____
 ___\n\nParking\n\nPaid visitor parking is available along Lomita Drive as 
 well as on the first floor of the Roth Way Garage Structure\, located at t
 he corner of Campus Drive West and Roth Way at 345 Campus Drive\, Stanford
 \, CA 94305. From the Palo Alto Caltrain station\, the Cantor 
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-53251196125393@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261021T221217Z
DTSTART:20261120T013000Z
DTEND:20261120T030000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Holly Herndon & Mat Dryhurst: Protocol Art
LOCATION:McMurtry Building\, Oshman Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/studio-lecture-series-holly-herndon-m
 at-dryhurst
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/studio-lecture-series-holly-h
 erndon-mat-dryhurst\n報名/票券: https://hollyherndonxmatdryhurst.event
 brite.com\n\nMade possible by the Millicent Greenwell Clapp Studio Art Ser
 ies Fund\, this series invites an artist each quarter for a two-day visit 
 consisting of studio critiques with our MFA students and an evening public
  lecture. This series continues to provide a dynamic platform for artists 
 to engage with the Stanford community\, fostering critical dialogue and cr
 eative exploration.\n\nProtocol Art\n\nIn this lecture\, Herndon and Dryhu
 rst discuss projects from their expansive practice and their concept of Pr
 otocol Art\, an approach that treats the creation of and intervention in t
 he systems\, protocols and rules shaping cultural production as an artisti
 c medium.\n\nHolly Herndon and Mathew Dryhurst are Berlin-based artists re
 nowned for their pioneering work in music\, machine learning\, and governa
 nce. Their practice creates precedent-setting projects where technical sys
 tems are artworks unto themselves\, operating at the intersection of art\,
  technology\, and infrastructure — work they describe as Protocol Art: i
 nterventions at the level of systems and protocols rather than objects\, a
 rguing for agency at the infrastructure layer.\n\nTogether they run Herndo
 n Dryhurst Studio\, and have co-produced critically acclaimed albums inclu
 ding Platform (4AD/RVNG 2015) and PROTO (4AD/2019)\, and developed Holly+\
 , a protocol for shared ownership and licensing of an artist's identity an
 d intellectual property.\n\nIn 2022\, they co-founded Spawning\, an organi
 zation that attempted to build a web-scale data permissions p
END:VEVENT
