SUMMARY:[現場] Global Health Research Methods Workshop
LOCATION:Stanford Research Park
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/global-health-research-methods-worksh
 op-2026
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/global-health-research-method
 s-workshop-2026\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLS
 eq6JTQbPFLjaK4MlVNDR1emvOabtonfYKdn0-SFiAe7W8UsA/viewform\n\nThis two day 
 all-day\, in-person workshop is for Stanford* School of Medicine fellows\,
  residents\, medical students\, and faculty interested in developing resea
 rch skills applicable to global health. The workshop provides a basic over
 view and roadmap to help people interested in conducting global health res
 earch develop their study question into a concept note that can form the b
 asis for a study proposal.  The workshop focuses on essential skills to de
 velop a competitive proposal and budget\, including how to approach global
  health research opportunities\, how to engage with collaborators\, consid
 eration of sample size\, and analytical approach.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-53418724495078@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20260818T205659Z
DTSTART:20270605T220000Z
DTEND:20270606T000000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Workshop with Saif Azzuz
LOCATION:O'Donohue Educational Farm
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/workshop-with-saif-azzuz
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/workshop-with-saif-azzuz\n報
 名/票券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/workshop-with-saif-azzuz\n\nJoi
 n us for an afternoon of artmaking with Saif Azzuz\, 2026-27 Doerr Visitin
 g Artist\, and cultural fire practitioner Elizabeth Azzuz. In this all age
 s\, family friendly workshop\, the Azzuzs will share the significance of c
 ultural fire\, or prescribed burns led by Indigenous practitioners to stew
 ard healthy ecosystems. Participants will create connections between nativ
 e flora and fauna\, and make pigments and drawings with charcoal from cult
 ural fire burns.\n\nThis program takes place on the O’Donohue Family Sta
 nford Educational Farm at 555 Fremont Road\, Stanford\, CA\, and is presen
 ted in conjunction with the Further Triennial exhibition California Curren
 t\, on view at the Cantor from October 29\, 2026 through 2028\, which look
 s at the ecological\, infrastructural\, personal\, creative\, and activist
  networks that shape life in the region. Visit California Current to see w
 orks by Azzuz\, which include charcoal drawings made from similar processe
 s.\n\nAll public programs at the Cantor Arts Center are always free! Space
  for this program is limited\; advance registration is recommended.\n\nRSV
 P here.\n\nAbout the Presenters\n\nSaif Azzuz (b. 1987\, born in Eureka\, 
 CA) is a Libyan-Yurok artist who resides in Pacifica\, CA. He received a B
 achelor’s Degree in Painting and Drawing from the California College of 
 the Arts in 2013. Working in painting\, sculpture and installation\, Azzuz
 ’s work reimagines and examines our relationships to nature\, privatizat
 ion and commodification. The use of different mediums all
