SUMMARY:[現場] Pediatric Otolaryngology Updates
LOCATION:Oceano Hotel & Spa
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/pediatric-otolaryngology-updates
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/pediatric-otolaryngology-upda
 tes\n報名/票券: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P
 =5&EID=57459\n\nOverview\nThe goal of this activity is to provide learners
  with current\, evidence-based advances and best practices in pediatric ot
 olaryngology. Through expert-led lectures and panel discussions\, faculty 
 will address a broad range of clinical topics\, including hearing screenin
 g and management of hearing loss\, foreign bodies of the ear\, nose\, and 
 throat\, airway disorders\, sleep-disordered breathing and obstructive sle
 ep apnea\, voice and swallowing disorders\, microtia\, and pediatric head 
 and neck masses. Additional topics will include the evaluation and managem
 ent of epistaxis\, ankyloglossia (tongue tie)\, and ear molding. The progr
 am is designed to enhance clinicians’ knowledge\, diagnostic skills\, an
 d application of contemporary approaches to the care of pediatric patients
  with otolaryngologic conditions.\n\nRegistrationPhysicians: $495.00\nNurs
 es/APP/Allied Health: $395.00\nIndustry: $595\nNon-Stanford Trainees (Resi
 dents & Fellows): $75.00\n\nTrainee Verification: When completing your pro
 file\, select Fellow/Resident as your Profession\, your NPI number in Cred
 entials\, and your Residency Program name in the Organization field.\n\nCr
 editsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (10.00 hours)\, ASHA CEU (0.10 hours)\,
  Non-Physician Participation Credit (10.00 hours)\, Speech-Language Pathol
 ogy Contact Hours (10.00 hours)\n\nTarget AudienceSpecialties - Otolaryngo
 logy (ENT)\, PediatricsProfessions - Audiologist\, Fellow/Resident\, Non-P
 hysician\, Physician\, Speech Language Pathologist ObjectivesAt the conclu
 sion
END:VEVENT
