LOCATION:Anderson Collection\, Wisch Family Gallery
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/curator-led-talk-surfacing-feb
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/curator-led-talk-surfacing-fe
 b\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSftIcUgvsEFDBmP
 bKXiAFiKnkydy7locRoYqCZpw1L-DoaQzw/viewform?usp=header\n\nJoin Kelsey Chen
 \, Exhibition Co-Curator\, on this special tour of surfacing.  \n\nRSVP HE
 RE\n\npatty chang: surfacing engages the ocean as a physical\, geopolitica
 l\, and symbolic space. The exhibition culminates a year-long residency th
 rough the Denning Visiting Artist program\, during which Chang was embedde
 d at Stanford’s Hopkins Marine Station. Incorporating fish specimens\, a
 rchaeological remains\, archival materials documenting the lives of Chines
 e fisher families in the early 1900s\, and a porcelain table that travels 
 from the Metropolitan Museum of Art to take new form at the Anderson\, Cha
 ng’s sculptural practice surfaces the mysterious intimacies and unrecord
 ed histories that haunt the Pacific Ocean and its coast. surfacing is the 
 first solo artist exhibition commission for Stanford’s Asian American Ar
 t Initiative (AAAI). \n\nThe exhibition will be on view in the Wisch Famil
 y Gallery from September 17\, 2026 – February 8\, 2027.
