SUMMARY:[現場] AUDITIONS | "Angels in America Part One: Millennium Approa
 ches"
LOCATION:Roble Gym
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/Angels-Auditions
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/Angels-Auditions\n報名/票
 券: https://taps.stanford.edu/angels-auditions/\n\nWINTER 2027 MAIN STAGE
  | LEARN MORE | View 26-27 Season\n\nWritten Tony Kushner | Directed by TA
 PS Graduate Student Connor Lifson\n\nABOUT Angels in America Part One: Mil
 lennium Approaches\nAs the AIDS crisis intensifies in the mid-1980s\, a gr
 oup of New Yorkers find their lives colliding in unexpected and extraordin
 ary ways. Just as intimate as it is epic\, Angels in America\, Part One: M
 illennium Approaches blends raw emotion\, political history\, queer identi
 ty\, love\, loss\, fantasy\, and\, of course\, angels. Relationships fract
 ure and bloom as characters confront illness\, abandonment\, ambition\, an
 d the possibility of transformation. Fiercely funny and deeply moving\, To
 ny Kushner’s monumental play explores what it means to survive in a shat
 tering world. This Production will serve as our annual TAPS 122P course of
 fering\n \n\nThe Graduate Repertory 2027 piece Cowboy Mouth will also seek
  actors from these auditions.
END:VEVENT
