DTSTAMP:20260821T195430Z
DTSTART:20261113T040000Z
DTEND:20261113T053000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] MAIN STAGE | Our Town
LOCATION:Roble Gym\, Elam Theater
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/our-town
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/our-town\n\nFALL MAIN STAGE 2
 026 | Tickets on Sale NOV 2026 | NO LATE SEATING\n\nWritten By Thornton Wi
 lder| Directed by Guest Artist Jeffrey Lo\n\nA Stage Manager enters before
  us calling for time. But it’s not a rehearsal they are calling us in fo
 r\, it’s real life. In Thornton Wilder’s masterwork Our Town we experi
 ence life in three acts: “Daily Life\,” “Love and Marriage” and fi
 nally\, “Death and Eternity.” In a world where the possibility of huma
 nity losing its grasp on reality looms large\, the resonance of this class
 ic reverberates today as strongly as it did when first written and in one 
 of those most stunning scenes in the American cannon\, we come face to fac
 e with what it is we have already lost.\n\nHailed by Edward Albee as “th
 e greatest American play ever written\,” this enduring story continues t
 o ask us—generations later—how to use our time\, how to love our time 
 and how to run out of time.
END:VEVENT
