SUMMARY:[線上] ENT Experts Up Close: Updates in Parotid Masses and Sinona
 sal Malignancies
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/ent-experts-up-close-updates-in-parot
 id-masses-and-sinonasal-malignancies
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/ent-experts-up-close-updates-
 in-parotid-masses-and-sinonasal-malignancies\n報名/票券: https://stanf
 ord.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=57310\n\nOverviewThis one-
 hour CME activity offers a concise\, evidence-based update on the evaluati
 on\, diagnosis\, and management of parotid masses and sinonasal malignanci
 es. Topics cover contemporary imaging\, pathology interpretation\, surgica
 l approaches\, as well as adjuvant and systemic therapies. The session emp
 hasizes multidisciplinary decision-making\, functional outcomes (including
  facial nerve preservation and skull base considerations)\, survivorship\,
  and select endoscopic and minimally invasive techniques. Attendees will l
 eave with useful takeaways to support clinical decision-making\, streamlin
 e referrals\, and stay current on evolving treatment options and clinical 
 trials.\n\nRegistrationRegistration for all practitioners - free\n\nTo reg
 ister for this activity\, please click HERE.\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 
 Credits™ (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participation Credit (1.00 hours)\
 n\nTarget AudienceSpecialties - Allergy\, Immunology\, and Rheumatology\, 
 Otolaryngology (ENT)Professions - Advance Practice Nurse (APN)\, Fellow/Re
 sident\, Non-Physician\, Nurse\, Physician\, Registered Nurse (RN)\n Objec
 tivesAt the conclusion of this activity\, learners should be able to:\n1. 
 Describe types of molecular testing available for parotid masses \n2. Revi
 ew the contraindications and indications for parotidectomy\n3. Identify up
 dates in diagnostic workup and staging criteria for sinonasal malignancies
 \n4. Describe emerging systemic therapies and active clinical trials relev
 ant to sinonasal cancer management\n\nAccr
END:VEVENT
