SUMMARY:[混合] HAI Seminar The AI 100
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building\, 119
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-seminar-with-mike-wooldridge-the-
 ai-100
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-seminar-with-mike-wooldri
 dge-the-ai-100\n線上連結: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN
 _OeOA7YGwQ8qGOfBdrTXx6w#/registration\n報名/票券: https://hai.stanford
 .edu/events/mike-wooldridge-the-ai-100\n\nAI Goes Mainstream: The Scaling 
 Era and the Rise of Generative AI\n\nMichael Wooldridge\, Ashall Professor
  of the Foundations of Artificial Intelligence\, University of Oxford\n\nM
 oderated by: Russ Altman\, Kenneth Fong Professor and Professor of Bioengi
 neering\, of Genetics\, of Medicine\, of Biomedical Data Science\, Senior 
 Fellow at the Stanford Institute for Human-Centered AI and Professor\, by 
 courtesy\, of Computer Science\n\nThis talk will cover key insights from t
 he third AI100 report\, AI Goes Mainstream: The Scaling Era and the Rise o
 f Generative AI\, set for release in October 2026. The report was commissi
 oned by the AI100 standing committee and led by study panel chair Michael 
 Wooldridge.\n\nWooldridge will discuss how generative AI achieved World Wi
 de Web-level impact in five years\, largely unanticipated even by its deve
 lopers\; why software engineering became AI's first killer app and what th
 at suggests for knowledge work\; the unprecedented scale of AI infrastruct
 ure investment and the strains it creates\; and the shift away from pure s
 caling toward reasoning and inference-time compute. He will also cover the
  concentration of frontier development among a small number of US and Chin
 ese actors\, expert disagreement over AGI timelines\, and a governance lan
 dscape that remains fragmented.\n\nThe One Hundred Year Study on Artificia
 l Intelligence (AI100) is a longitudinal effort administered out of Stanfo
 rd HAI and managed by a standing committee of AI experts from around the w
 orld\, chaired b
END:VEVENT
