SUMMARY:[現場] Lunchtime Curator Talk | California Current: Art and Histo
 ries from the Bay Area
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center\, Freidenrich Family Gallery (221)
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-lunchtime-curator-talk-califo
 rnia-current-art-and-histories-from-the-bay-area-7503
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-lunchtime-curator-tal
 k-california-current-art-and-histories-from-the-bay-area-7503\n報名/票
 券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/rgPHwqPV\n\nJoin Maggie Dethloff\, Ass
 istant Curator of Photography and New Media\, on this special tour of Cali
 fornia Current: Art and Histories from the Bay Area.\n\nRSVP here.\n\nHow 
 does a community stay rooted in a region that’s constantly changing? Cal
 ifornia Current invites you to consider this question and others through i
 ts more than 60 works — many on view for the first time — that explore
  the interplay between Bay Area history\, art\, and artists over the past 
 century.\n\nTitled after the major cold-water current that runs the length
  of the West Coast of North America\, California Current brings together p
 aintings\, sculptures\, works on paper\, photographs\, and time-based medi
 a by Bay Area artists from the twentieth century to the present. The exhib
 ition traces a series of interconnected currents — ecological\, infrastr
 uctural\, technological\, personal\, creative\, and political — that hav
 e shaped both artistic production and everyday life in Northern California
 .\n\nArranged thematically across time and media\, California Current plac
 es historical works in conversation with contemporary ones\, emphasizing b
 oth continuity and change. Together\, they ask: What has drawn so many peo
 ple to this region? What has allowed communities and creative practices to
  take root here? And what continues to keep so many of us — despite the 
 Bay Area’s contradictions\, pressures\, and constant reinvention — dee
 ply connected to this place? Presented as part of the Further Triennial\, 
 this exhibition features works by arti
END:VEVENT
