SUMMARY:[現場] "Tracing Mindfulness Back to Its Sources": T. T. and W. F.
  Chao Workshop with Bhikkhunī Dhammadinnā and Paul Harrison
LOCATION:Alumni Center\, McCaw Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/tracing-mindfulness-back-to-its-sourc
 es-t-t-and-w-f-chao-workshop-with-bhikkhuni-dhammadinna-and-paul-harrison
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/tracing-mindfulness-back-to-i
 ts-sources-t-t-and-w-f-chao-workshop-with-bhikkhuni-dhammadinna-and-paul-h
 arrison\n\nThis workshop is a part of the T. T. & W. F. Chao Buddhism and 
 Contemporary Society Series and will explore the early Buddhist sources of
  mindfulness meditation in theory and in practice. Participants will be gu
 ided through an examination of the teachings that form the shared inherita
 nce of all later Buddhist traditions and that also inform many contemporar
 y applications. Throughout the day\, we will be looking into multiple cons
 tructs and perspectives on mindfulness and their practical implications\, 
 discovering how theory\, practice\, and their interweaving have continuall
 y evolved—shaped by diverse maps and goals of the Buddhist path across t
 ime\, through different cultures\, and into present-day recontextualizatio
 ns.\n\n​The workshop will offer participants the opportunity for experie
 ntial exploration of the relevant practices together with an accessible sc
 holarly grounding in the primary textual sources in translation.\n\n​Thi
 s event is free and open to the public\, and everyone is welcome. However\
 , because of space limitations\, registration is essential. Registration w
 ill close on November 10. Some prior exposure to basic Buddhist or mindful
 ness teachings and practices is helpful but not a prerequisite for partici
 pation.\n\nPlease register here. \n\n​Schedule:\n\n​Morning Session\n\
 n​09:00–09:10 Introduction\n\n​09:10–09:20 Guided Meditation\n\n
 ​09:20–10:00 The Four Foundations of Mindfulness (satipaṭṭhāna) i
 n Theory & Practice: An Overview\n\n​10:00–10:30 Discussion\n\n​10:3
 0–10:45 Short Break\n\n
END:VEVENT
