SUMMARY:[混合] 36th Annual Jonathan J. King Lecture: Dr. Bryant Lin & Dr.
  Shoshana Ungerleider
LOCATION:Cedar Room\, Stanford Faculty Club\, Cedar Room
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/36th-annual-jonathan-j-king-lecture
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/36th-annual-jonathan-j-king-l
 ecture\n線上連結: https://med.stanford.edu/bioethics.html\n報名/票
 券: https://StanfordKingLecture.eventbrite.com\n\nThe Girand Center for B
 iomedical Ethics is pleased to announce this year’s speaker\, Dr. Bryant
  Lin\, in conversation with Dr. Shoshana Ungerleider\, for the 36th Annual
  Jonathan J. King Lecture.\n\nWe invite you to join us on Thursday\, Novem
 ber 5 at 5:30pm PT in the Cedar Room at the Stanford Faculty Club or via l
 ivestream for My Cancer Journey: Happiness and Sadness\, Hope and Fear. \n
 \nIn this talk\, Dr. Lin will share a candid and deeply personal reflectio
 n on living with terminal cancer. As a leading researcher\, cancer advocat
 e\, and patient\, he brings a rare perspective to the realities of serious
  illness\, clinical care\, hope\, and what it means to live fully in the f
 ace of uncertainty. Joining Dr. Lin is Dr. Shoshana Ungerleider\, a physic
 ian\, journalist\, producer\, and leading voice in compassionate\, patient
 -centered care. Together\, Dr. Lin and Dr. Ungerleider will explore the em
 otional and practical dimensions of a cancer diagnosis—including fear\, 
 purpose\, relationships\, and the ways we navigate life-limiting illness w
 ith honesty and humanity.\n\nSpecial book launch opportunity: In-person at
 tendees will have the opportunity to purchase signed copies of Dr. Lin’s
  new book\, Sunshine: An Exploration of Living When You Are Dying\, releas
 ing November 10. Hors d’oeuvres and refreshments will also be served fol
 lowing the program.\n\nWe hope to see you there! \n\n \n\nAbout the speake
 rs\n\nBryant Lin\, MD\, MEng is a primary care physician\, educator and re
 searcher. The cornerstone of Dr. Lin's work i
END:VEVENT
