SUMMARY:[線上]   Alcohol-Associated Hepatitis and Early Liver Transplanta
 tion
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/alcohol-associated-hepatitis-and-earl
 y-liver-transplantation
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/alcohol-associated-hepatitis-
 and-early-liver-transplantation\n報名/票券: https://stanford.cloud-cme
 .com/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=59994\n\nOverviewThis activity reviews 
 the diagnosis and management of alcohol-associated liver disease (ALD) and
  alcohol-associated hepatitis (AAH)\, including alcohol cessation strategi
 es\, treatment of alcohol use disorder\, appropriate use of corticosteroid
 s\, and the evolving role of early liver transplantation. Learners will ga
 in practical guidance on risk stratification\, treatment thresholds\, and 
 timely referral of patients with severe alcohol-associated liver disease.\
 n\nRegistrationRegistration for all practitioners - free.\n\nTo register f
 or this activity\, please click HERE\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits
 ™ (1.00 hours)\, AAPA Category 1 CME credits (1.00 hours)\, ANCC Contact
  Hours (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participation Credit (1.00 hours)\n\nT
 arget AudienceSpecialties - Family Medicine & Community Health\, Gastroent
 erology\, Gastroenterology & Hepatology\, Hematology\, Internal MedicinePr
 ofessions - Advance Practice Nurse (APN)\, Non-Physician\, Nurse\, Physici
 an\, Physician Associate\, Registered Nurse (RN) ObjectivesAt the conclusi
 on of this activity\, learners should be able to:\n1. Apply NIAAA clinical
  criteria and phosphatidylethanol testing to accurately diagnose alcohol-a
 ssociated hepatitis and distinguish alcohol-associated liver disease from 
 MASLD.\n2. Use MELD rather than the Maddrey discriminant function to risk-
 stratify patients with alcohol-associated hepatitis and identify candidate
 s for corticosteroid therapy.\n3. Manage corticosteroid therapy appropriat
 ely\, including assessmen
END:VEVENT
