SUMMARY:[現場] An Evening of Poetry with Fady Joudah
LOCATION:Humanities Center\, Levinthal Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/an-evening-of-poetry-with-fady-joudah
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/an-evening-of-poetry-with-fad
 y-joudah\n報名/票券: https://stanforduniversity.qualtrics.com/jfe/form
 /SV_diiD3e2pMLJJWfk\n\nJoin us for a reading and conversation with Palesti
 nian American physician\, poet\, and translator Fady Joudah. Joudah is the
  author of […]. He has also published seven other collections of poems: 
 The Earth in the Attic\; Alight\; Textu\, Footnotes in the Order of Disapp
 earance\; Tethered to Stars\; and his newest collection: Exhibit G: Poems\
 , Essays\, and Photographs of Gaza (September 2026). Exhibit G is describe
 d as "a collection of poems\, essays\, and photographs that offer a Palest
 inian representation of not only the staggering grief\, but the unwavering
  resilience and prevailing life force of a people and place enduring genoc
 ide." \n\nJoudah has translated several collections of poetry from Arabic\
 , including several works by Mahmoud Darwish\, and he is the co-editor and
  co-founder of the Etel Adnan Poetry Prize. Winner of the Yale Younger Poe
 ts Prize\, he has received the Jackson Poetry Prize\, a PEN award\, the Sa
 if Ghobash Banipal Prize for Arabic Literary Translation\, the Griffin Poe
 try Prize\, a Guggenheim Fellowship\, Arab American Book Award\, the Lenor
 e Marshall Prize\, and the American Book Award. He lives in Houston\, with
  his wife and kids\, where he practices internal medicine.\n\nExhibit G wi
 ll be available for purchase and signing at the event.\n\nPlease RSVP to a
 ttend.
END:VEVENT
