SUMMARY:[現場] Korea’s Nuclear Odyssey Beyond Borders: From KEDO to the
  Age of AI
LOCATION:Encina Hall\, 3RD Floor\, Philippines Conference Room (C330)
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/koreas-nuclear-odyssey-beyond-borders
 -from-kedo-to-the-age-of-ai
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/koreas-nuclear-odyssey-beyond
 -borders-from-kedo-to-the-age-of-ai\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.co
 m/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScaj-7L8dHRpk31lkBqk8D7aRU-Tj35FrmvVhW_5u5KmFsJ-w/viewf
 orm\n\nEvery odyssey begins with a departure\, but the Odyssey is also a s
 tory of return—not just to where one began\, but to lessons learned alon
 g the way.\n\nSouth Korea’s nuclear journey beyond its borders spans thr
 ee landmark projects: KEDO in North Korea\, Barakah in the United Arab Emi
 rates\, and Dukovany in the Czech Republic. Each unfolded in a different i
 nternational environment\, from nonproliferation and energy cooperation to
  commercial competition and today’s renewed concerns over geopolitics an
 d energy security. Dr. Lim compares these projects to trace the evolution 
 of Korea’s nuclear export capabilities. As AI and data centers add new m
 omentum to nuclear energy\, she asks whether Korea’s path forward may ul
 timately lead back to an earlier lesson: the importance of international c
 ooperation.\n\nAbout the speaker:\n\nEunjung Lim is a visiting scholar at 
 APARC and professor in International Studies at Kongju National University
  in Korea. Her research focuses on international cooperation in the Indo-P
 acific\, comparative and global governance\, and energy\, nuclear\, and cl
 imate change policies in East Asia. She previously served as a board membe
 r of the Korea Institute of Nuclear Nonproliferation and Control (May 2018
 –July 2024) and as a member of the Subcommittee on Energy and Just Trans
 ition of the Presidential Commission on Carbon Neutrality and Green Growth
 . She currently serves as a member of the Policy Advisory Committee for th
 e Ministry of Unification and as a member of the govern
END:VEVENT
