SUMMARY:[線上] Artificial Intelligence Regulatory & Policy Landscapes
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/artificial-intelligence-regulatory-po
 licy-landscapes
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/artificial-intelligence-regul
 atory-policy-landscapes\n報名/票券: https://godort.libguides.com/frida
 ychats\n\nDate and Time: 10–11AM\, Friday\, November 6\, 2026Location: V
 irtual (zoom link provided upon registration)Instructor: Danielle Gensch (
 State\, Local\, and International Government Librarian)This seminar is par
 t of The American Library Association's Government Documents Roundtable (A
 LA-GODORT) Friday Chats series (https://godort.libguides.com/fridaychats).
  Please register through the ALA-GODORT website to receive the Zoom link.\
 n\nGenerative artificial intelligence is almost everywhere we look\, and r
 esearchers are considering its role and impact in a wide variety of fields
 . Several international\, state\, and local organizations provide policy a
 nd regulation repositories worth knowing about. Danielle Gensch\, State\, 
 Local\, and International Government Librarian at Stanford University Libr
 aries will provide a brief tour of OECD\, NCSL\, NLC\, and other helpful t
 ools in the government information librarian’s kit. She will focus on ke
 y topics like data centers\, energy\, sustainability\, and intellectual pr
 operty. Please feel free to bring your own examples\, particularly for fed
 eral resources\, generally outside the scope of Danielle’s work and her 
 slides.
END:VEVENT
