SUMMARY:[混合] Using AI to Find Sources
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing\, Velma Denning Room (120F)
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/using-ai-to-find-sources
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/using-ai-to-find-sources\n報
 名/票券: https://appointments.library.stanford.edu/event/17626269\n\nDa
 te and Time: 2–3PM\, Tuesday\, November 10\, 2026Location: Velma Denning
  Room (120F)\, Green Library & Virtual (zoom link provided upon registrati
 on)Instructor: Pauline Lewis (Reference and Instruction Librarian)Are you 
 using AI to find sources for your research project? Do you think you shoul
 d be but aren't sure how? Join this workshop and learn concrete tips about
  the possibilities and limitations of using GenAI to discover primary and 
 secondary sources. We'll explore how to thoughtfully use LLMs in this crit
 ical phase of your research and how to pair these new tools with tradition
 al methods of discovering and accessing sources. \n\nPlease register to at
 tend. Registration is exclusively open to current Stanford affiliates and 
 will be offered on a first-come\, first-served basis. For those attending 
 the in-person event\, please bring your Stanford ID card or mobile ID to e
 nter the library. Virtual attendees will receive a Zoom link upon registra
 tion.
