DTSTAMP:20261026T164807Z
DTSTART:20261119T200000Z
DTEND:20261119T213000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Galicia's Promised City with Oskar Czendze
LOCATION:Building 200\, History Corner\, 307
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/galicias-promised-city-with-oskar-cze
 ndze
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/galicias-promised-city-with-o
 skar-czendze\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1euIgnTpdatJ3
 oa1vsQCf_V0GapwEdC6A-0gqpPE_M68/edit\n\nBetween 1890 and 1914\, tens of th
 ousands of Jews from Galicia—the easternmost crownland of the Habsburg E
 mpire—made New York City their new home. Yet their distinct experience h
 as often been overshadowed by national narratives centered on migration fr
 om the Russian Empire. Oskar Czendze (University of Toronto) will explores
  how Galician Jews carried forms of regional and supranational belonging s
 haped in East Central Europe into New York. \n\nWhen: Thursday | Nov 19 | 
 12:00pm  \n\nWhere: Bldg. 200 | Rm. 307\n\n              \n\nRSVP required
 . Lunch included with RSVP.
END:VEVENT
