SUMMARY:[現場] Artist Talk | Holographic Space\, a talk by Charles Ray
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center\, Cantor Eastman Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/charles-ray
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/charles-ray\n報名/票券: h
 ttps://thethirdplace.is/event/charles-ray\n\nJoin us for an artist talk wi
 th renowned sculptor Charles Ray\, followed by a conversation with Patrick
  R. Crowley\, Associate Curator of European Art at the Cantor.\n\nFor over
  fifty years\, Charles Ray has worked towards the limits of sculpture\, ex
 ploring how the transformation of space can change a viewer's relationship
  to an object. Ray will reflect on his work over the decades\, including h
 is 16mm film Fashions (1996)\, which is currently on view in Solid Picture
 s.\n\nCurated by Patrick R. Crowley\, Solid Pictures is the first major ex
 hibition to explore the overlooked 1859 photosculptures of French artist a
 nd inventor François Willème\, whose experiments translating photographi
 c negatives into three-dimensional figures lay the groundwork for modern 3
 D scanning and printing technologies.\n\nCrowley will join Ray in conversa
 tion to discuss how Ray’s broader practice connects to the questions in 
 the exhibition around three-dimensionality\, consumerism\, and how clothin
 g and fashion sit within the perceptual understanding of a figure.\n\nAll 
 public programs at the Cantor Arts Center are always free! Space for this 
 program is limited\; advance registration is recommended. Those who have r
 egistered will have priority for seating.\n\n​RSVP here.\n\nAbout the Ar
 tist\n\nCharles Ray (b. 1953) grew up in Chicago and moved to Los Angeles 
 in 1981\, where he currently lives and works. His art has been featured in
  Documenta\, three Venice Biennales\, and six Whitney Biennials\, and his 
 sculptures have been the s
END:VEVENT
