SUMMARY:[現場] Tracing What Remains: Memory\, Place\, and Chinese America
 n Histories
LOCATION:Anderson Collection\, Denning Family Resource Center
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/tracing-what-remains-memory-place-and
 -chinese-american-histories
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/tracing-what-remains-memory-p
 lace-and-chinese-american-histories\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.co
 m/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf8K9K_f55rlureRm8AbFnJ8YkMQsXCDllfpsdkWjyLMuhYAg/viewf
 orm?usp=preview\n\nPresented in conjunction with Patty Chang's surfacing\,
  Tracing What Remains: Memory\, Place\, and Chinese American Histories bri
 ngs together films that examine the histories of Chinese communities acros
 s Northern California through landscape\, memory\, and acts of remembrance
 . Moving between documentary\, historical narrative\, and poetic reflectio
 n\, these films trace the enduring presence of communities whose lives and
  labor were systematically erased from the historical record.\n\nFrom the 
 displaced Chinese fishing villages of the San Francisco Bay to the expulsi
 on of Chinese residents from Eureka\, these works reveal how places can ho
 ld memory even when official histories do not. Together\, they ask how art
 ists can recover forgotten stories\, map absences\, and imagine new ways o
 f bearing witness to the past.\n\nFollowing the screening\, filmmakers\, C
 hisa Hughes (Many Moons) and Rene Yung (Chinese Whispers) will join in con
 versation with surfacing co-curator\, Kelsey Chen to discuss filmmaking as
  a practice of historical recovery\, the relationship between place and me
 mory\, and the ongoing work of preserving Chinese American histories.\n\nR
 SVP HERE\n\nFilms\n\nMany Moons \n\n2023 | 21:43 minutes\n\nIn the county 
 which once boasted it was “free of Chinamen\,” Chinese community membe
 rs search for those who may have survived Humboldt's 1885 expulsion and 60
  years of enforced exclusion– the only known survivor being Charlie Moon
 \, whose descendants are Native tribal members. Framed by the words of a g
 host
END:VEVENT
