SUMMARY:[現場] What is a Public Intellectual Today: Alexis Madrigal
LOCATION:Tresidder Union\, Oak Lounge
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/what-is-a-public-intellectual-today-a
 lexis-madrigal
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/what-is-a-public-intellectual
 -today-alexis-madrigal\n報名/票券: https://stanforduniversity.qualtric
 s.com/jfe/form/SV_cHIH2DzsPVcgrm6\n\nPlease join us for the autumn event o
 f the Stanford Public Humanities flagship speaker series\, What Is a Publi
 c Intellectual Today\, which will feature journalist Alexis Madrigal. He w
 ill be in conversation with Adrian Daub on craft\, career\, and culture in
  the Bay Area and beyond. Book signing and selling to follow for both auth
 ors. \n\nPlease RSVP at this link to attend the event. \n\nAlexis Madrigal
  is an acclaimed multimedia journalist in Oakland\, CA. He is the co-host 
 of KQED’s current affairs show Forum\, creator of the 8-part podcast Con
 tainers\, author of the newsletter The Oakland Garden Club\, and a contrib
 uting writer at The Atlantic\, where he co-founded The COVID Tracking Proj
 ect. His book The Pacific Circuit explores how a logistical revolution tha
 t began in Oakland has reshaped American cities. He is the proprietor of L
 ocal Economy\, a community space in Oakland\, and has been a visiting scho
 lar at UC Berkeley’s School of Information and the Center for Science\, 
 Technology\, Medicine & Society. \n\nAdrian Daub is J.E. Wallace Sterling 
 Professor in the Humanities at Stanford University\, where he serves as th
 e Faculty Director of the Clayman Institute for Gender Research. He is the
  author of What Tech Calls Thinking (2020) and The Cancel Culture Panic (2
 024)\, and writes for numerous US and European newspapers and magazines.\n
 \nThis event is cosponsored by the Department of Communication\, the Journ
 alism Program\, the Michelle R. Clayman Institute for Gender Research\, th
 e Stanford Of
END:VEVENT
