 ealthy-aging
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/2027-annual-conference-in-men
 opause-healthy-aging\n報名/票券: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course
 /courseoverview?P=5&EID=59455\n\nOverviewThis conference will equip you wi
 th the knowledge and tools to support your patients through the menopause 
 transition and beyond. You'll learn from experts how to manage symptoms of
  perimenopause and menopause — hot flashes\, sleep and mood disturbances
 \, cognitive changes\, sexual dysfunction\, skin and hair issues - plus ho
 w to address long term priorities like bone health\, heart health\, breast
  cancer risk and the role of supplements.\n\nRegistrationThe webinar will 
 be presented live on Pacific Standard Time. All sessions will be recorded 
 and the recordings will be provided to all registrants to review until Aug
 ust 31\, 2027\, including those who were not able to attend any of the liv
 e sessions.\n\nRegistration fee includes course materials\, certificate of
  participation\, and the webinar recordings. \n\nYou will receive the Zoom
  information the week before the webinar. If you register within a week of
  the webinar\, you will receive the Zoom information on Tuesday\, March 9t
 h. \n\nEarly Bird Rates:\nPhysician - $495\nRN/AHP/Other:  $350\nNurse Pra
 ctitioner (NP): $350\nNurse Rn/APRN: $350\nPA: $350\nPsychologist: $350\nS
 ocial Worker: $350\n\nRegistration Rate After 12/10/2026:\nPhysician - $69
 5\nRN/AHP/Other:  $450\nNurse Practitioner (NP): $450\nNurse Rn/APRN: $450
 \nPA: $450\nPsychologist: $450\nSocial Worker: $450\n\nRegistration fees m
 ay be paid by credit card - Visa\, MasterCard\, or American Express. Your 
 email address is used for critical information\, including registration co
 nfirmation\, evaluation
END:VEVENT
