 uthor Francisco Jiménez. The film follows his family's journey as immigra
 nt farmworkers in California: a childhood working in the fields\, the stru
 ggle to attend school\, and a close-knit family's constant fear of deporta
 tion.\n\nThe screening will be followed by a fireside chat between Francis
 co Jiménez\, Professor Emeritus at Santa Clara University\, and Tomás Ji
 ménez\, Professor of Sociology and Founding Faculty Director of the Insti
 tute for Advancing Just Societies at Stanford University. A Q&A will follo
 w with Francisco Jiménez and members of the production team: Josh Peterso
 n (Director and Screenwriter)\, Normandie Ramirez (Executive Producer)\, a
 nd Robin Mortarotti (Creative Consultant and Producer).\n\nFrancisco Jimé
 nez is the author of the memoir series The Circuit\, Breaking Through\, Re
 aching Out\, and Taking Hold. The series is recognized among the American 
 Library Association's 50 Best Young Adult Books of All Time.\n\nLearn more
  about the film at theunbrokensky.com.\n\nSponsors: Center for Latin Ameri
 can Studies. Co-sponsored by Chicana/o-Latina/o Studies (CCSRE) and El Cen
 tro Chicano y Latino.\n\nRSVP for the event\n\nFrancisco Jiménez\, Author
  & Professor Emeritus\n\nFrancisco Jiménez\, Professor Emeritus at Santa 
 Clara University\, emigrated from Mexico to California as a child and work
 ed alongside his family as m
END:VEVENT
