SUMMARY:[現場] Pediatric Grand Rounds (CME): When Governments Swipe Left:
  Australia’s Social Media Policy
LOCATION:Center for Academic Medicine \, Grand Rounds Room 
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-pediatric-grand-rounds-cme-ne
 onatology-40-reimagining-newborn-brain-care-in-the-era-of-digital-health
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-pediatric-grand-round
 s-cme-neonatology-40-reimagining-newborn-brain-care-in-the-era-of-digital-
 health\n\nWhen Governments Swipe Left: Australia’s Social Media Policy\n
 \n \n\nPRESENTER\nSusan Sawyer\, MD\nGeoff and Helen Handbury Chair of Ado
 lescent Health\nThe University of Melbourne\nSpeaker Profile\n\n \n\nSESSI
 ON DESCRIPTION\nNearly one year ago\, Australia became the first country i
 n the world to implement highly controversial national legislation that at
 tempted to reduce children’s exposure to social media. This presentation
  will describe the background to the Australian legislation\, outline the 
 approach that the government is taking to its evaluation\, and share the l
 atest data about what the legislation has - and has not - achieved. In doi
 ng so\, the overarching objective of this presentation is to encourage ref
 lection on how health professionals\, parents\, communities and government
 s best respond to the rapidly changing digital and commercial determinants
  of child and adolescent health.\n\n\n\nEDUCATION GOALS\n\nUnderstand the 
 context of social media as a commercial determinant of child and adolescen
 t health.Consider the range of available policy responses to counter the c
 ommercial determinants of Health.Reflect on your personal beliefs and bias
 es in relation to public policy around children's exposure to social media
 .\n LOCATION (in-person)\nCenter for Academic Medicine\nGrand Rounds Room\
 n453 Quarry Road\, \nPalo Alto\, CA 94304\n\n \n\nZOOM INFORMATION\nRegist
 er to attend this session via Zoom here.\n\nSubscribe to receive weekly em
 ail announcements and Zoom webinar information for each session.\nSubscrib
 e
END:VEVENT
