SUMMARY:[現場] The Body as Monument
LOCATION:El Centro Chicano\, Jaime Miranda Lounge
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-body-as-monument
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-body-as-monument\n報名/
 票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdAiJ9dXkNqtkRMdUe_UdICul
 KlKXMHSq0krQoMLzfc2wQ7tw/viewform\n\nChicana/o-Latina/o Studies and El Cen
 tro are thrilled to welcome Jess Sabogal\, a cuir Colombian - American mur
 alistx and printmaker from San Francisco whose large-scale public artworks
  attempt to document and disrupt. \n\nIn this artist talk\, Jess Sabogal m
 aps a two-decade creative evolution\, expanding from the monumental scale 
 of muralismo and printmaking into intimate self-portraiture and sculpture.
  Guided by the relationships and histories that sustain their practice\, S
 abogal examines the shifting weight of an artist’s responsibility. They 
 explore lineage\, radical representation\, and the urgency of creating wor
 k for communities whose bodies and futures remain at risk for erasure.\n\n
 For the past 10 years\, Sabogal has consistently reinvented what it means 
 to be a muralistx in a male-dominated medium. She has continuously pushed 
 the boundaries as an artist by utilizing her medium for social change\, ac
 tion and empowerment. Her murals have been commissioned by Facebook\, Goog
 le\, 20th Century Fox\, the University of Southern California\, the Univer
 sity of California\, The University of Arizona\, and The University of Uta
 h among many others. Sabogal’s work has been featured in national and in
 ternational news and media sources including CNN\, The Wall Street Journal
 \, The Huffington Post\, and the New York Times.\n\nPlease RSVP ~ lunch wi
 ll be provided!
END:VEVENT
