SUMMARY:[現場] Physics\, Politics\, and Pakistan
LOCATION:Black Community Services Center
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/physics-politics-and-pakistan
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/physics-politics-and-pakistan
 \n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScLcLSwRC8SeHJ08
 GHjRsbZPNGHJjufAxwn38Er2KL6CNwTNw/viewform\n\nThis event is co-sponsored b
 y The Center for South Asia\, The Sara and Sohaib Abbasi Program in Islami
 c Studies and The Markaz Resource Center.\n\nJoin us for a conversation on
  where Pakistan's democracy stands\, what secularism could mean there\, an
 d what the current political moment demands of not just Pakistan but also 
 the global South. The CSA-Markaz Academic Fellow invites you to Physics\, 
 Politics\, and Pakistan with Dr. Pervez Hoodbhoy\, a distinguished Pakista
 ni physicist\, public intellectual\, and longtime advocate for science\, r
 ationalism\, and secular thought.\n\nPervez Amirali Hoodbhoy born in Karac
 hi (1950)\, resides in Islamabad where he taught physics for 47 years (197
 3-2021) at Quaid-e-Azam University. From 2013-2020 he was Distinguished Pr
 ofessor of Physics and Mathematics at Forman Christian College-University\
 , Lahore. Earlier\, for short periods he was visiting professor at MIT\, C
 arnegie Mellon University\, the University of Maryland\, and a post-doctor
 al researcher at the University of Washington. In 2022 he founded The Blac
 k Hole\, a community space in Islamabad dedicated to the pursuit of scienc
 e\, art\, and culture.
END:VEVENT
