SUMMARY:[混合] Relational Intelligence (RQ): Building Relational Futures 
 in the Age of AI
LOCATION:Building 120\, McClatchy Hall\, Main Quad\, Studio S40 - bring you
 r Stanford ID card/mobile ID to enter the building
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/relational-intelligence-rq-building-r
 elational-futures-in-the-age-of-ai
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/relational-intelligence-rq-bu
 ilding-relational-futures-in-the-age-of-ai\n線上連結: https://youtube.
 com/live/0FahuE94C3U?feature=share\n線上資訊:\nSign up for the webinar
  here: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_FhoD1uNcSEOf5dBb6-gZN
 g#/registration\n報名/票券: https://cvent.me/VE7w48\n\nJoin the Tech I
 mpact and Policy Center on November 10th from 12PM–1PM Pacific for a sem
 inar with Isabelle Hau.\n\nStanford affiliates are invited to join us at 1
 1:40 AM for lunch\, prior to the seminar. The Fall Seminar Series continue
 s through December\; see our Fall Seminar Series page for speakers and top
 ics. Sign up for our newsletter for announcements.\n\nAbout the Seminar:\n
 \nAs AI reshapes how we learn\, work\, and connect\, understanding and str
 engthening human relationships has become an urgent scientific and societa
 l priority. This session invites researchers across disciplines to explore
  Relational Intelligence (RQ)\, our capacity to build trust\, cultivate be
 longing\, navigate differences\, and form meaningful connections. Together
 \, we will examine emerging scientific questions\, identify opportunities 
 for interdisciplinary research\, and imagine new ways to measure\, develop
 \, and strengthen relational capacities. How might we build a future in wh
 ich advances in artificial intelligence are matched by advances in human c
 onnection?\n \n\nAbout the Speaker:\n\nIsabelle C. Hau is the executive di
 rector of the Stanford Accelerator for Learning\, where she brings togethe
 r learning & brain science\, technology\, and innovation to advance effect
 ive\, inclusive\, and human-centered approaches to learning.\n\nPreviously
  an impact investor\, Isabelle led the U.S. education practice at Omidyar 
 Network and Imaginable Futures\, investing in mission-driven organizations
  that have reached millions of learners. 
END:VEVENT
