SUMMARY:[現場] SLAC on Tap: Night of the Dark Matter
LOCATION:The Dutch Goose
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/slac-on-tap-night-of-the-dark-matter
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/slac-on-tap-night-of-the-dark
 -matter\n報名/票券: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/slac-on-tap-night-of-
 the-dark-matter-tickets-2003218031056?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true\n\nS
 omething is lurking in the dark.\n\nDark matter makes up most of the matte
 r in the universe\, yet it continues to slip through our grasp. But could 
 scientists be closing in? The LUX-ZEPLIN (LZ) experiment recently made hea
 dlines after researchers spotted a mysterious particle interaction that th
 ey can’t easily explain – one that could potentially have been caused 
 by dark matter. Meanwhile\, SuperCDMS has started its hunt for lighter dar
 k matter particles with detectors sensitive enough to pick up their fainte
 st traces.\n\nAt this special Halloween edition of SLAC on Tap\, four SLAC
  scientists will take us deep into the bowels of the Earth\, where experim
 ents like LZ and SuperCDMS have set traps for one of the universe’s snea
 kiest substances. We’ll explore what could be hiding in the dark\, how s
 cientists are trying to catch it and what it would take to finally unmask 
 dark matter.\n\nThe event will include a moderated panel followed by an au
 dience Q&A. Come dressed as your favorite dark matter candidate for our co
 stume competition: WIMPs\, axions and other mysterious particles are all w
 elcome. The dark is waiting.\n\nAbout Dan Akerib\, Tom Shutt\, Kelly Stift
 er and Ann Wang\n\nDan Akerib and Tom Shutt\, both professors of particle 
 physics & astrophysics at SLAC\, have been working together in the search 
 for dark matter for most of the last 30 years\, starting with the CDMS pro
 gram and continuing through the development of liquid-xenon dark matter de
 tectors\, including LUX and LZ.\n\nWhen Dan and Tom
END:VEVENT
