SUMMARY:[現場] Emerging String Quartet Program – The Dolphins
LOCATION:Braun Music Center\, Campbell Recital Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/esqp-dolphins-quartet
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/esqp-dolphins-quartet\n\nThe 
 Dolphins Quartet performs as part of the Emerging String Quartet Program (
 ESQP).\n\nThe Dolphins Quartet is a string quartet and composer collective
  united by a belief that chamber music can be vibrant\, daring\, and deepl
 y human. Trained at Juilliard and based in New York City\, the quartet has
  gained recognition for adventurous programming\, original compositions\, 
 and performances that reimagine the possibilities of quartet playing. In A
 pril 2026\, they won Gold Prize and Audience Prize at the Chesapeake Chamb
 er Music Competition\, establishing their presence as a world-class ensemb
 le in the classical music scene. Read more here!\n\n \n\nMembers:\nLuke He
 nderson – violin\nIsaac Park – violin\nJames Preucil – viola\nIan Ma
 loney – cello\n\nThe ESQP provides a young ensemble opportunities simila
 r to what the St. Lawrence String Quartet\, ensemble in residence at Stanf
 ord University from 1998-2024\, enjoyed in their early years through an in
 tensive week of community outreach. The up-and-coming musicians gain valua
 ble experience performing for varied audiences in a short period of time w
 hile the greater Stanford community benefits from the input of energy and 
 contact with the young ensemble.\n\nAmission Information\n\nFree admission
 Parking permits are required for weekday campus parking. We recommend down
 loading the ParkMobile app before arriving.
END:VEVENT
