SUMMARY:[線上] Holding the Line: Setting Boundaries for Yourself and Othe
 rs This Holiday Season
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/holding-the-line-setting-boundaries-f
 or-yourself-and-others-this-holiday-season
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/holding-the-line-setting-boun
 daries-for-yourself-and-others-this-holiday-season\n報名/票券: https:/
 /stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=60415\n\nOverviewThe
  holiday season can bring a particular kind of pressure for families carin
 g for a child with medical complexity or navigating life after loss — fr
 om well-meaning relatives who don't understand care routines to social obl
 igations that feel impossible to meet. This session brings together a pane
 l of parents\, some currently caregiving and some bereaved\, to talk hones
 tly about what it looks like to protect your time\, energy\, and peace dur
 ing this time of year. Panelists will share how they've learned to say no\
 , to ask for the support they actually need\, and to hold firm boundaries 
 with extended family\, friends\, and even well-intentioned strangers. The 
 conversation will also explore the added layer bereaved parents carry — 
 navigating traditions\, invitations\, and other people's expectations of g
 rief — while still honoring their own family's story. Join Courageous Pa
 rents Network for a candid\, supportive discussion offering practical lang
 uage and permission to protect what matters most this season.\n\nRegistrat
 ionRegistration for all practitioners - free\n\nTo register for this activ
 ity\, please click HERE.\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (1.00 hou
 rs)\, ACPE Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, ANCC Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, 
 APA Continuing Education credits (1.00 hours)\, ASWB Continuing Education 
 (ACE) credits (1.00 hours)\, CDR Continuing Professional Education Units (
 1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participation Credit (1.00 hours)\, Occupation
 al Therapy Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, Phy
END:VEVENT
