SUMMARY:[現場] Filmmaker Kahlil Joseph\, In Conversation
LOCATION:McMurtry Building\, Oshman Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/filmmaker-kahlil-joseph-in-conversati
 on
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/filmmaker-kahlil-joseph-in-co
 nversation\n報名/票券: https://luma.com/shf38g4b\n\nKahlil Joseph on t
 he Representation of Space and the Making of the Underground Museum\n\nJoi
 n acclaimed filmmaker and artist Kahlil Joseph for a public conversation e
 xploring the representation of space in his films\, including the construc
 tion of Black space in his latest feature-length work\, BLKNWS: Terms and 
 Conditions. The conversation will also examine how these ideas take shape 
 beyond the screen through the creation of Los Angeles’s acclaimed Underg
 round Museum\, a visionary cultural space dedicated to Black art\, thought
 \, and creative expression\, which Joseph co-founded in 2012 alongside his
  family artists Noah Davis and sculptor Karon Davis. \n\nThis event is par
 t of the Art and Art History Course An Architectural Imagination taught by
  Christian Ho as well as part of the ongoing work by Kahlil Joseph\, BLKNW
 S on view as part of the permanent collection at the Harmony House\, home 
 of the Institute for Diversity in the Arts. \n\nWhen: November 10\, 2026\,
  5:30–8:00 p.m. \nWhere: Oshman Hall\, McMurtry Art Building. \n\nPresen
 ted by: Department of Art and Art History Institute for Diversity in the A
 rts Department of African and African American Studies Documentary Film an
 d Video Program The Anderson Collection With special support from Jennifer
  DeVere Brody\, Professor of Theater and Performance Studies and\, by cour
 tesy\, of African and African American Studies.
END:VEVENT
