DTEND:20261113T050000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] MRC Public Lecture: Tadashi Tokieda
LOCATION:GSB Knight - Arbuckle / Cemex\, Cemex Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/mrc-public-lecture-tadashi-tokieda
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/mrc-public-lecture-tadashi-to
 kieda\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeGj8Br_-rX
 KmiwkZ_h2qhBqgQqH5YwW1drPkYg8G9ajpl_ng/viewform\n\nIf planning to attend\,
  please submit an RSVP here.\n\nThe Stanford Mathematics Research Center p
 resents Surprises from rubbing the wrong way\, a lecture given by Tadashi 
 Tokieda\, Professor of Mathematics at Stanford University\, as part of the
  MRC Public Lecture series.\n\nFriction\, stickiness\, jamming . . . Don
 ’t we frown on these conditions as spoilers of life? This lecture\, howe
 ver\, will perform baffling experiments that pop out of these conditions\,
  and probe their subtle physics via simple mathematics. You’ll be able t
 o enjoy many of the experiments with friends and family as easy magic.\n\n
 Tadashi Tokieda is starting his 10th year as a member of the Stanford math
  department\, after vagabonding across careers — painter\, philologist\,
  precarious plumber\, physicist. He likes to collect counter‑intuitive p
 henomena which he discovers\, designs\, or learns about from others\, and 
 to share them in outreach\, e.g. via the YouTube channel Numberphile. T^2 
 spoke in that capacity at the quadrennial International Congress of Mathem
 aticians 2018\, 2022\, 2026.\n\nThis lecture is free and open to the publi
 c.\n\nSee the full event poster here.\n\nYou can find more information abo
 ut speaker Tadashi Tokieda on the Stanford Math Department website.
END:VEVENT
