SUMMARY:[線上] CREATE Webinar - Modality: A Case Study in Implementing AI
  in Clinical Practice
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/modality-case-study-implementing-ai-c
 linical-practice
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/modality-case-study-implement
 ing-ai-clinical-practice\n報名/票券: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/
 register/WN_I1t4vA50SfKKUcGDTQq1aQ\n\nJoin us on November 4\, 12–1pm PT 
 for a roundtable discussion exploring what it takes to move an AI-enabled 
 behavioral health tool from development into real-world clinical practice\
 , using Modality as a case study. Speakers from Modality\, clinical partne
 r Cornerstone Treatment Facilities Network\, and research partner Stanford
  University will discuss how teams build trust and organizational buy-in\,
  integrate new tools into existing workflows\, and navigate challenges rel
 ated to adoption\, usability\, privacy\, safety\, and potential bias. The 
 conversation will also highlight the roles of clinical\, technical\, resea
 rch\, and implementation partners\, lessons from real-world deployment\, a
 nd ongoing efforts to understand engagement\, fidelity\, and impact over t
 ime - offering a behind-the-scenes look at what it takes to move promising
  technology toward meaningful\, sustainable use in practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54251654190408@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261015T232427Z
DTSTART:20261111T200000Z
DTEND:20261111T210000Z
SUMMARY:[線上] Mental Health Technology + Innovation Hubinar: Integrating
  AI into Virtual Reality for Mental Health Care (Panel)
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/integrating-ai-virtual-reality-mental
 -health-care
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/integrating-ai-virtual-realit
 y-mental-health-care\n報名/票券: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/regi
 ster/WN_Y3GhpEwnSK6pqqjhaTntVA\n\nJoin us on November 11th\, 12-1pm PT for
  a panel on "Integrating AI into Virtual Reality for Mental Health Care".\
 n\nVirtual and augmented reality are increasingly being used to deliver ex
 posure-based treatments for anxiety related disorders\, trauma\, addiction
 \, and other mental health conditions. Advances in artificial intelligence
  are now expanding what these technologies can do\, enabling more interact
 ive\, adaptive\, and personalized therapeutic experiences. In this panel\,
  experts spanning clinical research and digital health will explore the ev
 olving role of AI in virtual and augmented reality for mental health care.
  Panelists will share examples of AI-enabled tools designed to address rea
 l-world clinical needs\, including interactive virtual characters\, person
 alized exposure environments\, and systems that can adapt treatment based 
 on patient response. \n\nThe discussion will examine where AI can meaningf
 ully enhance therapeutic XR\, what aspects of human interaction and real-w
 orld exposure these technologies are unable to replicate\, and how clinici
 ans can remain appropriately involved as systems become more adaptive. Pan
 elists will also consider the guardrails needed for responsible use\, the 
 potential role of wearable data in personalization\, and the practical cha
 llenges of moving promising tools from research and development into evide
 nce-based clinical practice.
END:VEVENT
