DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/shenson-recital-rachel-willis
 -sorensen\n報名/票券: https://live.stanford.edu/s/event?EventID=32601\
 n\nSoprano Rachel Willis-Sørensen is joined by pianist Tamar Sanikidze fo
 r a recital of late Romantic songs by Rachmaninoff\, Sibelius\, and Straus
 s\, along with dramatic 20th-century selections by Korngold\, Kander\, and
  Previn. A regular presence at the Metropolitan Opera and an audience favo
 rite at San Francisco Opera\, Willis-Sørensen has been hailed by the San 
 Francisco Chronicle for her “heroic power and tenderness.” Especially 
 noted as a Strauss interpreter\, she was recently honored with the Beverly
  Sills Artist Award and made her Carnegie Hall recital debut.\n\nThe Shens
 on Recital Series is generously funded by the Ben and A. Jess Shenson Fund
 s at Stanford University.\n\nAdmission Information\n\nTickets: $16.00 – 
 $95.04
