SUMMARY:[現場] LECTURE | LUXURY LINER
LOCATION:Roble Gym\, Lounge
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/lecture-luxury-liner
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/lecture-luxury-liner\n報名/
 票券: https://forms.gle/soQokP2qZmoaCoh98\n\nLECTURE | RSVP HERE | Open 
 to Stanford Community\n\nFor this talk of Port Call\, Georg Dahled will pr
 esent a slideshow of Luxury Liner\, featuring several late arrivals and ne
 w contributions. It will begin with a brief introduction\, followed by the
  slideshow\, which guests are invited to explore informally while enjoying
  refreshments and engaging in conversation. The gathering will conclude wi
 th a moderated conversation and Q&A with the artist\, facilitated by Pauli
 ne Mornet\, PhD candidate in Performance Studies at Stanford University.\n
 \nThe event will occur at Roble Lounge in Roble Gym\, Stanford on October 
 29 from 12–2pm. Light refreshments will be served.\nThis event is co-spo
 nsored by the Department of Theater & Performance Studies and the Departme
 nt of Art & Art History.\n\nABOUT LUXURY LINER\n\nLuxury Liner is a projec
 t developed by artist Georg Dahled between June 2025 and June 2026\, explo
 ring language\, travel\, and the fragility of translation. During this per
 iod\, Dahled travelled extensively. At numerous stops along his journeys\,
  he mailed vintage postcards sourced from flea markets and antique shops t
 o recipients around the world. Each card bears a stamped sentence that doc
 uments his attempts to learn or approximate the language of the place from
  which it was sent. As he appears to be in the process of learning and exp
 erimenting with each language\, misspellings\, grammatical errors\, and mi
 stranslations accumulate and mutate\, turning linguistic failure into both
  method and material
END:VEVENT
