SUMMARY:[線上] Using AI to Listen\, Learn\, and Act on Community Feedback
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/using-ai-to-listen-learn-and-act-on-c
 ommunity-feedback
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/using-ai-to-listen-learn-and-
 act-on-community-feedback\n報名/票券: https://ssir.org/webinars/entry/
 ai-community-feedback\n\nMeaningful change begins with listening. Evidence
  shows that when we genuinely understand people’s needs and act on what 
 we hear\, we make better decisions that lead to better outcomes. So how ca
 n AI help nonprofits and foundations listen to more people\, synthesize la
 rge volumes of data\, and respond more effectively? Join SSIR and Feedback
  Labs for a 90-minute interactive session exploring AI for feedback and li
 stening at scale. \n\nBuilding on Feedback Labs’ research and experience
 \, we’ll hear case studies from nonprofits and foundations that are usin
 g AI to accelerate and scale listening without losing the nuance\, trust\,
  and human connection that make listening meaningful. Participants will di
 scuss what’s working\, what’s not\, and what responsible AI-enabled li
 stening can look like in practice. Whether you’re already experimenting 
 with AI for listening or just beginning to explore its potential\, you’l
 l leave with practical ideas and questions to help you determine where AI 
 can\, and can’t\, strengthen your organization’s feedback and listenin
 g practices. \n\nJoin this interactive 90-minute program led by Alexis Ban
 ks\, Director of Learning and Operations at Feedback Labs\, and Annie Grie
 r\, Director of Community and Equity at Feedback Labs. \n\nYou can expect 
 to: \n\nWalk away with an understanding of how to think about effective an
 d responsible AI use in the context of community listening.Learn from peer
 s who are using AI to accelerate\, scale\, and strengthen their feedback p
 rocesses.Iden
END:VEVENT
