SUMMARY:[線上] Stanford Medicine Neurosurgery Master Class: Motion Preser
 vation of the Spine
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/stanford-medicine-neurosurgery-master
 -class-motion-preservation-of-the-spine
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/stanford-medicine-neurosurger
 y-master-class-motion-preservation-of-the-spine\n報名/票券: https://st
 anford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=0&EID=60418\n\nOverviewThis a
 ctivity will educate physicians on motion-preserving spinal surgery\, incl
 uding cervical and lumbar disc arthroplasty\, as an alternative to fusion.
  Participants will learn to identify appropriate surgical candidates\, und
 erstand contemporary techniques and technologies used in complex\, multile
 vel\, and revision spinal reconstructions\, and apply current evidence to 
 patient counseling and clinical decision-making.\n\nPresenter: Anand Veera
 vagu\, MD\, Professor of Neurosurgery\, Stanford Univeristy\n\nRegistratio
 nRegistration for all practitioners - free.\n\nTo register for this activi
 ty\, please click HERE\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (1.00 hours
 )\, Non-Physician Participation Credit (1.00 hours)\n\nTarget AudienceSpec
 ialties - Internal Medicine\, Primary Care & Population Health\, Sports Me
 dicineProfessions - Non-Physician\, Physician ObjectivesAt the conclusion 
 of this activity\, learners should be able to:\n1. Describe the indication
 s and patient selection criteria for motion-preserving spinal surgery (e.g
 .\, cervical and lumbar disc arthroplasty) versus fusion-based approaches\
 n2. Identify the surgical techniques and technologies used in complex spin
 al reconstructions\, including multilevel and revision cases\n3. Evaluate 
 strategies for avoiding and managing complications associated with motion 
 preservation and complex reconstructive procedures\n4. Apply current evide
 nce and long-term outcomes data to guide decision-making in complex spine 
 cases requiring reconstruction\n\nAccredi
END:VEVENT
