UID:stanford-54302138029167@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261021T162518Z
DTSTART:20261210T013000Z
DTEND:20261210T030000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Print Revolutions: Chinese Impressions\, 1630s–1960s\, w
 ith Clarissa von Spee (Curator\, Cleveland Museum of Art)
LOCATION:McMurtry Building\, Oshman Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/print-revolutions-chinese-impressions
 -1630s1960s-with-clarissa-von-spee-curator-cleveland-museum-of-art
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/print-revolutions-chinese-imp
 ressions-1630s1960s-with-clarissa-von-spee-curator-cleveland-museum-of-art
 \n\nIn August 2025\, the Cleveland Museum of Art (CMA) and the Metropolita
 n Museum of Art (the Met) announced the acquisition of well over 200 rare\
 , 18th century Suzhou woodblock prints from the collection of Christer von
  de Burg. The purchase brings some of the most sophisticated Chinese color
  prints to the United States\, enabling both institutions to tell the stor
 y of printmaking\, in combination with their world-class painting collecti
 ons\, in new ways and innovative displays.\n\nThe talk will introduce the 
 exhibition\, Print Revolutions: Chinese Impressions\, 1630s–1960s at the
  CMA  (15 November\, 2026 - 4 April\, 2027)  showcasing some of the finest
  exemplars of Chinese printmaking\, many of them seen in public for the fi
 rst time. More than eighty prints\, paintings\, and porcelains from the mu
 seum’s collection\, as well as a few loans\, illustrate the development 
 of color printing from the 1600s leading up to the international modern wo
 odcut movement in the early 1900s.  \n\nClarissa von Spee\, PhD\, is Chair
  of the Department of Asian Art and James and Donna Reid Curator of Chines
 e Art\, as well as Interim Curator of Islamic Art at the Cleveland Museum 
 of Art. \n\nImage: Gusu Beauty–Mother and Son in a Summer Pavilion (姑
 蘇美人 – 夏日亭畔母子圖)\, 1736–95. Southeast China\, Suzhou
  Qing dynasty (1644–1911)\, Qianlong period (1736–95). Polychrome wood
 block print\; ink and color on paper\; print only: 104.2 x 54.5 cm (41 x 2
 1 7/16 in.)\; overall: 112.9 x 62.9 cm (44 7/16 x 24 3/4 in.). The Clevela
 nd Museum of Art
END:VEVENT
