SUMMARY:[線上] Pediatric Pulmonology in the Primary Care Setting
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/pediatric-pulmonology-in-the-primary-
 care-setting
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/pediatric-pulmonology-in-the-
 primary-care-setting\n報名/票券: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course
 /courseoverview?P=5&EID=60362\n\nOverviewPediatric primary care providers 
 play an important role in diagnosing and managing children and young adult
 s with pulmonary conditions. In this webinar\, primary care providers will
  learn more about difficult to diagnose and treat pulmonary conditions tha
 t they may see in their practice. These could include severe or atypical a
 sthma\, recurrent or persistent pneumonia\, sleep disorders (account for a
 bout 40% of all pulmonary referrals)\, abnormal chest radiographs\, and ch
 ronic cough. Providers will leave this webinar with the ability to diagnos
 e and provide daily management of these conditions and learn also when to 
 consider consulting with a pediatric pulmonary specialist for advice.\n\nR
 egistrationRegistration for all practitioners - free\n\nTo register for th
 is activity\, please click HERE.\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (
 1.00 hours)\, AAPA Category 1 CME credits (1.00 hours)\, ANCC Contact Hour
 s (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participation Credit (1.00 hours)\n\nTarget
  AudienceSpecialties - PediatricsProfessions - Advance Practice Nurse (APN
 )\, Non-Physician\, Nurse\, Physician\, Physician Associate ObjectivesAt t
 he conclusion of this activity\, learners should be able to:\n1. Identify 
 common patient and caregiver education needs related to the management of 
 pediatric asthma\n2. Discuss how to proceed when a patient has an unclear 
 asthma diagnosis or difficult-to-treat asthma\n3. Identify how to treat pa
 tients with recurrent pneumonia\n4. Define how to approach treating chroni
 c cough
END:VEVENT
