SUMMARY:[現場] Stanford in Haus Cramer: A Berlin Microhistory - Book Laun
 ch and Reception
LOCATION:Humanities Center\, Levinthal Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/stanford-in-haus-cramer-a-berlin-micr
 ohistory-book-launch-and-reception
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/stanford-in-haus-cramer-a-ber
 lin-microhistory-book-launch-and-reception\n\nPlease join the DLCL Departm
 ent of German Studies for the Stanford in Haus Cramer: A Berlin Microhisto
 ry book launch. Featuring a presentation with editors Karen Ruoff Kramer a
 nd Cheryce von Xylander\, and Faculty Emeritus Larry Friedlander. Receptio
 n to follow. We are delighted to invite you to join us for a celebration o
 f the book’s release and of the Stanford in Berlin community on campus a
 nd beyond! The book\, published to mark the 50th anniversary of the Berlin
  Bing Overseas Studies Program\, offers a deep dive into the rich history 
 of the program\, the house\, and the city. Through its vast collection of 
 perspectives and materials\, it showcases Haus Cramer as witness to Berlin
  modernity\, to Jewish-German life between the wars\, and as a refuge for 
 those who lived\, taught\, and studied in its rooms. Take a look at the St
 anford Library’s Spotlight Exhibit and find the book at Stanford Univers
 ity Press. We look forward to the celebration and to bringing together Ber
 lin communities past\, present\, and future! RSVP for the book launch here
 . Respond by October 26 to secure your spot - limited seating available!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54311544929707@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261022T175451Z
DTSTART:20261117T010000Z
DTEND:20261117T023000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Book Talk: Prof. Cécile Alduy in Conversation with Prof. 
 Josh Landy
LOCATION:Building 260\, Pigott Hall\, Rm 216
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/book-talk-prof-cecile-alduy-in-conver
 sation-with-prof-josh-landy
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/book-talk-prof-cecile-alduy-i
 n-conversation-with-prof-josh-landy\n\nThe French and Italian Department a
 nd French Speaking Worlds: Here and Now present: A Book talk on D’abord 
 ils sont venus chercher les mots [First They Came for Words]\, les Arènes
 \, 2026\, by Prof. Cécile Alduy\, in conversation with Prof. Joshua Landy
 . \n\nAn Author Caught Up by Her Subject\nA professor of literature at Sta
 nford and a discourse analysis scholar\, Cécile Alduy has spent years ana
 lyzing how the far right wages its culture war. In 2022\, in La Langue de 
 Zemmour (Zemmour’s Language)\, she showed how the presidential candidate
  was distorting concepts and history to short-circuit rational thinking an
 d appeal to hatred and fear. Then\, on January 20\, 2025\, her research ca
 ught up with her brutally. At Stanford\, her life and work were upended\, 
 like those of colleagues\, students and workers in universities\, schools\
 , administrations\, and scientific labs nationwide\, when the new administ
 ration unleashed terror and censorship on culture and science. In this fir
 st-person account\, she tells what the far right does once in power\, day 
 to day.\n\nA New Linguistic and Political Regime\n“Women\,” “climate
  crisis\,” “disability\,” “diversity\,” “Black\,” “equalit
 y\,” “gender\,” “social justice\,” “LGBT\,” “prejudice\,
 ” “racism\,” “vaccine” ... These words\, among others\, have bee
 n banned or blacklisted by the Trump administration since March 2025. Céc
 ile Alduy conducts a gripping investigation into this list\, which grew fr
 om a handful of demonized terms into over 480 flammable ones through antic
 ipatory 
END:VEVENT
