DTSTART:20270226T010000Z
DTEND:20270226T023000Z
SUMMARY:[混合] Distinguished Lecture Series| From Disentanglement to Re-E
 ntanglement: Integrating the Living Archaeological Record
LOCATION:Building 500\, Archaeology Center\, 106
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/distinguished-lecture-series
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/distinguished-lecture-series\
 n線上連結: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_Euv4s6fIRyiB3h
 eE7WKV0Q\n\nEach quarter\, the Stanford Archaeology Center invites promine
 nt archaeologists from around the globe to be in residence for a week as a
  Distinguished Lecturer. During their residency\, the Distinguished Lectur
 er gives two lectures and interacts with faculty\, postdoctoral scholars a
 nd students. Stanford Archaeology Center will host Prof. Christopher H. Ro
 osevelt from  Koc University over two days (Feb 24 and Feb 25 for the Wint
 er Quarter of this academic year. \n\nAbstract:\n \n\nRecent trends in arc
 haeological data management have focused on preserving\, linking\, compari
 ng\, and reusing datasets\, and rightly so. The expensive work of archaeol
 ogical practice is too often relegated to inaccessible files and legacy da
 tabases\, recoverable only when future opportunities afford revived engage
 ment. While legacy datasets are one clear challenge\, so too are living da
 tasets\, those still growing\, still under analysis. As archaeological pra
 ctice is increasingly specialized\, its domain-specific archives have incr
 easing difficulty speaking to one another. Ceramics\, small finds\, botani
 cal and faunal remains\, conservation records\, drawings\, photographs\, a
 nd spatial data accumulate in parallel systems that share an archaeologica
 l site but can otherwise become siloed. This happens to born-digital proje
 cts too. The Kaymakçı Archaeological Project (KAP) was born digital in 2
 014\; by 2026 its records were accessed across seventeen separate database
  forms\, on their way to legacy status.\n\nThis lecture prese
END:VEVENT
